  "source_hints": null,
  "history": null,
  "answer": "Three specialist-consultant RFPs explicitly identify the incumbent and address whether it may compete:\n\n| RFP | Incumbent or existing consultant | May it compete? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Santa Barbara County Employees’ Retirement System — private equity (2020)** | **Hamilton Lane** is the incumbent private equity consultant. | **Yes.** The RFP expressly invites it to rebid. [SBCERS RFP, p. 9](SBCERS__2020-Private-Equity-RFP.pdf) |\n| **Baltimore City Employees’ Retirement System — alternatives (2024)** | **Meketa Group** is the incumbent alternatives consultant. **Marquette Associates** is the separate general investment consultant. | **Meketa may submit a proposal; Marquette may not** compete in this alternatives search. [BCERS RFP, pp. 8–9](Baltimore_BCERS__RFP-Alternatives-Consultant-rev.pdf) |\n| **District of Columbia Retirement Board — real assets (2011)** | **The Townsend Group** is the incumbent real-assets specialist. The RFP also identifies **Meketa Investment Group** as general consultant and **Pantheon** as private-equity specialist. | **Yes.** Townsend is expected to respond; Meketa is also expected to respond. [DCRB RFP, pp. 3–4](DC_Retirement_Board__dcrb-rfp-real-assets-investment-consulting-services.pdf) |\n\nA related **Oklahoma TRS general/private-markets RFP** names **Meketa Investment Group** as its *existing private-markets back-office provider*, not as the incumbent for the consulting work being solicited. Its reporting, fee-validation and capital-call services are expressly outside this search; the RFP does not expressly say whether Meketa will bid. [Oklahoma TRS RFP, p. 10](Oklahoma_TRS__Investment.Consultant.RFP.adopted.by.Board.pdf)",
  "response_status": "completed",
